# Static Linux — offline ISO package list.
#
# Same live-session base as profiledir-online/packages.x86_64 (kernel, boot,
# filesystems, live GUI) PLUS every official-repo package referenced across
# packages/lists/*.list — base + all 4 environments + all 8 sabores + all 3
# privacy profiles — deduplicated. The idea: mkarchiso's pacstrap downloads
# them all into the live image's own pacman cache at build time, so
# Calamares' live `pacman -S` calls (basepkgs/entorno-pkgs/sabores/
# privacidad-apply) can resolve from that cache with no network at install
# time — that's what "offline" means here.
#
# NOT solved yet: this only gets packages INTO the live squashfs's cache.
# Wiring Calamares' target-chroot pacman calls to actually READ from that
# cache instead of hitting the network needs either a bind-mounted cache
# dir + a Cachedir override in the target's pacman.conf, or a local repo
# (repo-add) added to the target's pacman.conf before basepkgs runs. Neither
# is built yet — see ../README.md. Until then this ISO is offline-shaped,
# not offline-functional.
#
# 10 packages across packages/lists/*.list are AUR-only (paru, ttf-outfit,
# otf-space-grotesk, aylurs-gtk-shell, libastal-meta, davinci-resolve,
# thonny, heroic-games-launcher-bin, proton-ge-custom-bin, joplin-desktop,
# bridge-utils) and can't be pacstrapped here at all without a local repo —
# same problem as calamares itself, see ../README.md.

# ---- Kernel / boot -------------------------------------------------
base
linux
linux-firmware
mkinitcpio
mkinitcpio-archiso
amd-ucode
intel-ucode
efibootmgr
memtest86+
memtest86+-efi
syslinux
grub

